# Shell scripts keep LF line endings in every checkout: bash on Linux and macOS
# (and in WSL) cannot run a script with CRLF endings.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Batch files keep CRLF: cmd.exe misreads some constructs in LF batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Migrations keep LF in every checkout: sqlx refuses to start on a database whose applied migration's
# bytes differ, so a database made by a Windows build would not open with a Linux one.
*.sql text eol=lf
